Hi Kamarul,
I personally  prefer the model that adjusts for all of the covariates individually unless you have a very small sample size or a rare outcome.   Basically that is a much more flexible model than is assuming that the outcome is a linear function of the propensity score, and so I prefer it unless degrees of freedom are severely limited.

Thanks,
Liz


